Status: DONE
Milestone: Automatically open successful Studio video exports
Dependencies: 10_STUDIO_FEEDBACK.todo
Purpose: Let the user immediately view the processed video through their normal media player.

Tasks:
  [x] Preserve the actual completed export result across the worker boundary.
  [x] Dispatch the saved local file through the OS default application on the UI thread.
  [x] Never launch for cancellation/failure; report launch refusal without losing saved output.
  [x] Validate real encoded synthetic export, bound path, launch refusal and incomplete jobs.
  [x] Update documentation/context and commit only this feature's changes.

Acceptance criteria:
  A successful Studio VIDEO export opens its actual result once, after pipeline cleanup.
  The selected app comes from the system file association; no hardcoded player or shell command.
  Editable filename fields cannot redirect playback to a different file.
  Cancellation/failure never launches a player.
  A player-launch refusal is visible while the successful output remains saved.
  CLI stays Qt-free/noninteractive. Installer work remains paused; frozen documentary unchanged.

Completion evidence:
  46 focused Studio/runtime/video-export tests and Ruff pass.
  The existing real four-frame encoded export now verifies main-thread launch after tracker/
  renderer cleanup, exact bound output despite edited fields, spaces/# URI handling and refusal.
  Cancellation/failure regressions prove no player launch and no completed output.
  Player dispatch is mocked; no real camera or user media player is opened by automated tests.
  Frozen 977-page documentary PDF remains byte-identical.
  User reading/playback approval remains separate from implementation evidence.
